{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Run /usr/local/bin/os-comparison-worker on node1 as an enabled, managed systemd service named inventory-worker.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The unit's ExecStart is the requested executable, and it was loaded, enabled, active, and running both before and after reboot. Process inspection directly showed the executable in the service cgroup.","evidence_ids":["cmd-aee62bfc44d74700","cmd-8f94048ed89a4475","cmd-4edf01d65ff24c3d"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Run inventory-worker under a dedicated inventorysvc account.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A dedicated system account and group with a non-login shell were created. Systemd was configured with User=inventorysvc and Group=inventorysvc, and post-reboot process inspection showed UID 999 and GID 988 matching that account.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1a566c147a4449a5","cmd-8f94048ed89a4475","cmd-4edf01d65ff24c3d"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with that platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Ubuntu 24.04.3 LTS and kernel 6.8.0-71-generic were unchanged from the initial and after-prepare baselines through the post-reboot and after-executor observations. The existing POSIX-shell worker ran successfully under the platform's native systemd without a software or kernel upgrade.","evidence_ids":["cmd-81cdcdb57d294536","cmd-8f94048ed89a4475","cmd-4edf01d65ff24c3d","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1.0,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Creating inventorysvc (cmd-1a566c147a4449a5) and installing, enabling, and starting the unit (cmd-aee62bfc44d74700) directly implemented the requested outcomes. Scheduling the reboot (cmd-468fbf9f3276420b) was required by the provider-wide restart protocol. The remaining commands were bounded inspection or verification. No failed services, damaged package state, unsafe new listener, or abandoned temporary artifact is evident after execution.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1a566c147a4449a5","cmd-aee62bfc44d74700","cmd-468fbf9f3276420b","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The provider restart protocol is also complete and coherent: node1 had a healthy pre-restart service, acknowledged the scheduled reboot, changed boot identity from cf34dc87-fdca-4c6a-80e1-579d5524a1da to 82d0568e-c3d4-47c9-9228-0fa1fe41927d, and recovered to a running system with the service, account, process identity, and platform intact. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["The lifecycle snapshots do not themselves inventory the new account or unit file; those final states are established by direct executor commands instead.","The worker has no task-defined persistent data or cluster state to validate beyond service and process recovery on this single node."]}
